  <h2>Read, and cited</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Bundesarchiv, <em>Gedenkbuch — Opfer der Verfolgung der Juden unter der nationalsozialistischen Gewaltherrschaft in Deutschland 1933–1945</em></strong>, online edition, read 14 September 2026. Entries <a href="https://apps.bundesarchiv.de/gedenkbuch/en1100957">en1100957</a> (Jacob), <a href="https://apps.bundesarchiv.de/gedenkbuch/en909753">en909753</a> (Samuel), <a href="https://apps.bundesarchiv.de/gedenkbuch/en1100894">en1100894</a> (Oskar), <a href="https://apps.bundesarchiv.de/gedenkbuch/en1100801">en1100801</a> (Georg). Also the surname search returning 50 Leibholz entries, which is what showed the two family clusters.</li>
    <li><strong>MyHeritage</strong>, Defranceski family site, family tree 9 — 164 individuals and 648 facts, read 14 September 2026. The spine of this archive and the thing most of the work consists of checking.</li>
    <li><strong>MyHeritage DNA</strong> — ethnicity estimate and match list for Lynn Derrick Luwinski's kit, read 14 September 2026.</li>
    <li><strong>FamilySearch</strong>, <em>South Africa, Civil Marriage Records, 1840–1973</em> — Kurt Luwinski and Ivone de Figueiredo de Witt, 19 June 1948, Johannesburg, certificate 858 (<a href="https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:6ZHT-WSJM">1:1:6ZHT-WSJM</a>); Morris Isaac Salkow and Ivone Luwinski, 13 February 1953 (<a href="https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:6ZHR-B6Y3">1:1:6ZHR-B6Y3</a>). Hanover, Orange Free State records, for the 1956 marriage.</li>
    <li><strong>National Archives of South Africa (NAAIRS)</strong> — divorce actions of 1948, 1951 and 1957, cited in the family tree by reference.</li>
    <li><strong>Stolpersteine Berlin</strong> — checked for Leibholz stones; those found (Willmanndamm 6, Danckelmannstraße 44) belong to other Leibholz families.</li>
